    "https://jobs.montana.edu/": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Home Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Welcome to Montana State University ! Come and experience our remarkable setting and adventurous community of students, faculty and staff. Interested in seeing more of campus take our Virtual Walking Tour. Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. For technical assistance while applying, contact University Human Resources at (406)-994-3651 or email atshelpdesk@montana.edu. To view open positions, please choose a job type below: Faculty Staff Student Affiliates About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Strategic Plan Campus Civil Rights Montana State University commits to a learning and working environment that emphasizes the dignity and worth of every member of its community and that is free from unlawful discrimination and harassment. Consistent with MSU’s commitment, and with all applicable law, the University prohibits unlawful discrimination or harassment, including sexual misconduct prohibited by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, and will take appropriate action to prevent, resolve, and remediate the effects of protected-class harm. Learn more Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Act, a consumer protection law passed in 1990, requires all colleges and universities who receive federal funding to share information about crime on campus and their efforts to improve campus safety as well as inform the public of crime in or around campus. Learn more Labor Condition Application Notice Labor Condition Application Notices will be posted electronically for 10 business days. Veteran's Preference In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Learn more University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
